! A.frr — Pure provider (no upstream, no peers)
!
! Relationships (Gao-Rexford):
!   Customers: S (10.0.1.2), D (10.0.4.2)
!
! A has no provider and no peers — it only serves customers.
! Both S and D pay A for transit, so A provides full global reachability to both.
!
! Local preference:
!   300 = customer-learned
!
! Export policy (valley-free routing):
!   → customers: full table (they pay for global connectivity)

bgp community-list standard CUSTOMER-ROUTES permit 65001:100
!
ip prefix-list OWN-PREFIX seq 5 permit 10.255.1.1/32
!
! Inbound from customers: tag + prioritise
route-map FROM-CUSTOMER permit 10
 set community 65001:100
 set local-preference 300
!
! Outbound to customers: full table
route-map TO-CUSTOMER permit 10
!
router bgp __ASN__
 address-family ipv4 unicast
  neighbor 10.0.1.2 route-map FROM-CUSTOMER in
  neighbor 10.0.1.2 route-map TO-CUSTOMER out
  neighbor 10.0.4.2 route-map FROM-CUSTOMER in
  neighbor 10.0.4.2 route-map TO-CUSTOMER out
 exit-address-family
!
